-- title:
--   Adic completion commutes with quotients over a Noetherian ring
-- statement:
--   Let $N$ be a commutative Noetherian ring and let $I$ and $\mathfrak p$ be ideals of $N$. Write $\hat N =$ `AdicCompletion I N` for the $I$-adic completion of $N$, an $N$-algebra via the canonical map `algebraMap N (AdicCompletion I N)`, and let $\mathfrak p \hat N =$ `𝔭.map (algebraMap N (AdicCompletion I N))` be the ideal of $\hat N$ generated by the image of $\mathfrak p$. On the other side, let $\bar I =$ `I.map (Ideal.Quotient.mk 𝔭)` be the image of $I$ in $N/\mathfrak p$ and let $\widehat{N/\mathfrak p}$ be the $\bar I$-adic completion of $N/\mathfrak p$, again an algebra over $N/\mathfrak p$ by its canonical map. The assertion is that there exists a ring isomorphism $$e : \hat N/\mathfrak p\hat N \;\xrightarrow{\ \sim\ }\; \widehat{N/\mathfrak p}$$ which is compatible with the two structural maps out of $N$: for every $x \in N$, the image under $e$ of the class modulo $\mathfrak p\hat N$ of the canonical image of $x$ in $\hat N$ equals the canonical image of $x \bmod \mathfrak p$ in $\widehat{N/\mathfrak p}$. The isomorphism is asserted to exist with this compatibility property, not produced as a named map.
--
--   This is the standard exactness statement for adic completion over a Noetherian ring (completion of a quotient is the quotient of the completion), in the ring-theoretic form: for $N$ local with $I$ its maximal ideal it identifies the formal fibre $\hat N/\mathfrak p\hat N$ with the completion of $N/\mathfrak p$. It is used in the verification of smoothness of relative dimension one after base change to a residue field, where completions at primes are recognised as power series rings.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AdicCompletion_exists_ringEquiv_quotient_map_adicCompletion_quotient.lean

import Mathlib

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
